"1","GPIO","NA","gpio_reg_wr_rd_test","Read GPIO GP0 registers 8–27 and verify read operations complete successfully; capture values for mapped registers GPIO_8, GPIO_9, and GPIO_22.","Sequential register-read validation for GPIO GP0: For each listed register token, perform a read and apply a read_compare expectation (mask_hex=NA, value_hex=NA). Mapped registers include GPIO_8 (fields: G8_io_wr_mask, G8_dout_wr_mask), GPIO_9 (field: G9_io_wr_mask), and GPIO_22 (field: G22_io_wr_mask). Unmapped entries (GPIO_10–GPIO_21, GPIO_23–GPIO_27) are read without resolved register-name mapping. No write operations are performed.","NA","NA","NA","NA","GPIO0 instance is defined and active; read-only access.","1. Initialize access to the GPIO GP0 register block on the DUT.
2. Read GP0 GPIO registers 8 through 27 sequentially.
3. For mapped registers (GPIO_8, GPIO_9, GPIO_22), record the read values for analysis.
4. Confirm that all reads complete without access faults or compare errors.
